{"scenario":"dts-arq-ed3-long-cpdu-wraps","rows":["C-0166","C-0170","C-0178","C-0190","C-0194","C-0201","C-0207","C-0510","C-0512","C-0516","C-0552","C-0558","C-0730","C-0766","C-0771","C-0776","C-0778","C-0779","C-0794","C-0797","C-0798","C-1154","C-1190","B-0215","B-0232","C-1194","A-0321"],"source":"Ed4 C.4.4.1, p.C-23; C.4.5.4, pp.C-29 to C-30; C.5.1, pp.C-58 to C-60; C.7.2, pp.C-97 to C-100; C.7.3.2.1, pp.C-104 to C-105","description":"On an 8-bit link a C_PDU of 300 segments, more than the window and more than the modulus, is received over four bursts as its FSNs wrap from 255 to 0; the acknowledgements carry RX LWE and SELECTIVE ACKS across the wrap and the C_PDU is delivered once, whole.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":25,"block_ms":4800}]},"cas":{"max_links":4,"link_request_timeout_ms":60000,"link_request_retries":2,"first_data_timeout_ms":600000},"dts":{"ack_wait_ms":60000},"sis":{"soft_link_idle_ms":3600000,"soft_link_min_hold_ms":3600000,"soft_link_max_ms":3600000}},"note":"Link setup as dts-arq/ed3-family-roundtrip (the peer 0.0.1.3 is recorded Ed3, the link uses the 8-bit family, B-0232), except cas.first_data_timeout_ms 600000, so cas.first_data/0.0.1.3 starts at 57550 for 600000 ms and stops only when the C_PDU reaches the CAS (B-0215). The peer sends one DATA C_PDU of 1800 bytes (the 6-byte header of ed3-family-roundtrip and 1794 bytes, byte i being i mod 251) in 300 ED3-DATA-ONLY D_PDUs of 6 bytes each, 24 bytes a D_PDU, all with DELIVER IN ORDER, C_PDU START on the first and C_PDU END on the last, EOT 20. Nothing bounds a C_PDU's segments by the window or the modulus; consecutive segments take consecutive FSNs modulo 256 and are joined in that order (C-0510, C-0512, C-0516, C-0190, C-0558). Burst 1 (61000): FSNs 0 to 127, TX WIN LWE on 0 and UWE on 127, the most a sender may have outstanding (C-0771). RX LWE moves to 128, RX UWE 127 (C-0776, C-0778); nothing is complete. At 83000 (contention 12000, second draw) the ED3-ACK-ONLY carries RX LWE 128 and no SELECTIVE ACKS, 12 bytes, EOT 10, and one copy fills the 25-byte block (C-1154). Burst 2 (101000): FSNs 128 to 255 with 250 lost; LWE on 128, UWE on 255 (Equation 1 against RX UWE 127 and RX LWE + 127 = 255, C-0794). RX LWE stops at 250, RX UWE 255. At 156000 (contention 45000, third draw) the ACK-ONLY carries RX LWE 250 and one SELECTIVE ACKS byte 0x1f, bits for 251 to 255 from the LSB (C-0201, C-0207); 13 bytes, so no copy fits. Burst 3 (171000): the peer's retransmission of 250 is lost, and its new FSNs 0 to 43 (the 257th to 300th segments, UWE and C_PDU END on 43) arrive; 43 is within RX LWE 250 + 127 (Equation 1 and 3, C-0794, C-0798; C-0779). RX LWE stays 250 and RX UWE becomes 43: these are new FSNs, not copies of the 0 to 43 already received in burst 1, whose segments are held behind RX LWE for the C_PDU not yet complete. At 217000 (contention 36000, fourth draw) the ACK-ONLY carries RX LWE 250 and 49 bits for 251 to 255 and 0 to 43, all set: six bytes 0xff and 0x01, 19 bytes, no copy (C-1190: the bitmap runs across the wrap). Burst 4 (231000): FSN 250 with TX WIN LWE (Equation 2 against RX UWE 43 - 127 = 172 and RX LWE 250, C-0797). RX LWE passes 250 to 255 and 0 to 43 and stops at 44; the C_PDU is complete and RX LWE has passed its last segment, so it is delivered (C-0178): cas.first_data stops and S_UNIDATA_INDICATION carries the 1794 bytes to conn 1. At 274000 (contention 33000, fifth draw) the ACK-ONLY carries RX LWE 44, 12 bytes, with one copy. Fixture: 25 bytes and 4800 ms a block, so a one-block transmission lasts 5550 ms. Seed 0 draws uniform(16) = 15, 4, 15, 12, 11: contention waits 45000, 12000, 45000, 36000, 33000 ms (K-0080). Bytes were encoded by the reviewer's own encoder from Figures C-9 and C-11 and the CRCs of Code Examples C-1 and C-2, checked against ed3-family-roundtrip.  The soft link times are set to 3600000 so that no SIS close falls within the run; the SIS starts sis.soft_link_min_hold (called node only), sis.soft_link_max and sis.soft_link_idle when the link is made, and stops the idle wait while an ARQ U_PDU is outstanding (A-0320, A-0321, A-0326)."}
